  "label": "Textual Material: 'opens ice cream shop'",
  "description": "The phrase 'opens ice cream shop' is a common trope in memes and jokes, implying a business venture that is expected to offer a specific, popular product (ice cream). This phrase sets up an expectation that is then subverted by the second text. The humor relies on the audience understanding that 'ice cream shop' is a specific type of establishment, and the contrast with 'only sells shakes' is only funny if the viewer knows that ice cream shops typically offer more than just shakes. This requires cultural knowledge of common business expectations and food industry norms.",
